---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../islands/IntakeForm.svelte';
const relay = process.env.PUBLIC_NLD_RELAY ?? 'https://api.landback.land';
---

<Page
  title="Report an error"
  lede="If something here is wrong, tell us what and, if you can, a source that shows it."
>
  <p>
    Every record has an id (for example <code>TLA-T-369</code>) shown in its label. Including it
    helps. Primary sources are best: the treaty text, the Statutes at Large, a court opinion, a
    nation’s own website.
  </p>
  <IntakeForm client:load {relay} kind="correction" />
  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    We check the source, change the data, and log the change publicly in the repository’s data
    changelog. Corrections from a Native nation about itself are applied first and checked after.
  </p>
</Page>
